    "goal": "Characterize hanging-drop evaporation for a screen plating 3.48 µL drops at 34.7 °C and 62% RH, for an interior well (row F, col 5) over 0.185 h.",
    "rationale": "Hanging-drop evaporation follows the d²-law; the interior well (row F, col 5) has no plate-edge penalty (edge factor 1.0). At 34.7 °C / 62% RH the interior Langmuir evaporation rate is ~15.1 µL/h, so a 3.48 µL drop loses ~2.4 µL in 0.185 h, leaving ~1.1 µL. This is a rapid loss and must be checked against the assay's minimum working volume.",
